+--[[
+	Specs for PlacementRules. They test the public contract documented in PlacementRules.luau
+	(snap, validate, MaxHeight, MaxReach) and nothing else, so a refactor that keeps placement
+	working shouldn't break them.
+
+	Conventions:
+	- Each rejection test starts from the known-good request below and changes one input, so the
+	  rejection can only come from the rule under test. "accepts a valid request" proves the
+	  baseline is good.
+	- Rejection reasons are documented only as "a short reason for the server log", so the specs
+	  check that a reason string comes back, not its exact wording.
+	- Expected cells are written out as numbers, assuming BlockTypes.BlockSize = 4,
+	  PlacementRules.MaxHeight = 200 and PlacementRules.MaxReach = 24. If those values change,
+	  update the numbers here.
+	- Every test builds its own occupied table, so tests don't depend on run order.
+]]
+
